# Navigation Patterns

## Route Constants

Defined in `lib/core/routing/router.dart`:

```dart
class AppRoute {
  static const String splash = '/';
  static const String onboarding = '/onboarding';
  static const String login = '/login';
  static const String signUp = '/signUp';
  static const String bottomNavigation = '/bottomNavigation';
}
```

## Navigation Methods

Always use `AppRoute` constants — never string literals.

```dart
// Go to route (replaces current)
context.go(AppRoute.login);

// Push route (adds to stack)
context.push(AppRoute.signUp);

// With path parameters
context.push('${AppRoute.userDetail}/$userId');

// With extra data
context.push(AppRoute.editProfile, extra: userProfile);

// Go back
context.pop();
```

## Route Definitions

Configured in `lib/core/routing/router.dart`:

```dart
// Standard route
GoRoute(
  path: AppRoute.login,
  builder: (context, state) => const LoginView(),
),

// Route with custom transition
GoRoute(
  path: AppRoute.onboarding,
  pageBuilder: (context, state) => CustomTransitionPage(
    key: state.pageKey,
    child: const OnboardingView(),
    transitionsBuilder: (context, animation, secondaryAnimation, child) =>
        FadeTransition(opacity: animation, child: child),
  ),
),
```

## NEVER Use String Literals

```dart
// BAD
context.go('/login');
context.push('/signUp');

// GOOD
context.go(AppRoute.login);
context.push(AppRoute.signUp);
```
